null}, {"t_ms": 315763, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_011H6No1jRiv1h2uy3Ghrh8R", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 315763, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_011H6No1jRiv1h2uy3Ghrh8R", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 315763, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_016rfK8rdeHo6n9ZZ8JVXpzH", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "Payments errors after deploy: payments-worker rolled back to v3.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "Payments errors started after this morning's deploy. payments-worker v3.4.0 was unhealthy in production (error rate 0.18) across us-east, us-west, and eu-west. Rolled back to v3.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production; rollback reported VERIFIED and human-approved. A rollback attempt against payments-api (v5.1.0 -> v5.0.0) was denied by a human reviewer because the problem was in payments-worker; no change was made to payments-api. Follow-up: confirm error rate recovery and investigate v3.4.0 regression.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-sev2-2025-rollback"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 316363, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_016rfK8rdeHo6n9ZZ8JVXpzH", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-sev2-2025-rollback", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 316363, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016rfK8rdeHo6n9ZZ8JVXpzH", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 319330, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled back `payments-worker` to v3.3.0 and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Initial target was wrong:** I first rolled back `payments-api` to v5.0.0, but a human reviewer denied that rollback and said the problem was in `payments-worker`.\n- **Rollback:** `payments-worker` was unhealthy on v3.4.0 with an 18% error rate. I rolled it back to v3.3.0, the last release that was healthy in production. It is now healthy on v3.3.0 in all three regions with an error rate of 0.2%. The rollback was verified and approved by a human.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open as SEV2 against `payments-worker`. The summary records the rollback, the denied `payments-api` attempt, and the follow-up to investigate the v3.4.0 regression.\n\n`payments-api` is still on v5.1.0 with an 18% error rate, the same figure as `payments-worker` had before its rollback. The reviewer said the problem was not there, but that error rate is worth a look. I did not change it. Please confirm whether it needs its own rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01My25iwNqyTJKKw8DaVpVnK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01AGKWfcUwcZteFYyJB45dch", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01S4DDbeNySayS3P1ABGKG8V", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-service"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01P7FoLnzxTDKVmiK8SPho8T", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-service"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"sig